      "sourceTextSha256": "838d31eb14be2757129728a8faee124d705680a4af7d70d8c274a38df70be94c",
      "text": "Day 10 · Breakfast. Full-day excursion to the walkways of the Perito Moreno Glacier, including the “Safari Náutico” boat trip. Drive 80 km to Los Glaciares National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site preserving a vast area of the continental ice field, from which the Moreno, Onelli, Agassiz and Upsala glaciers descend. The Perito Moreno spreads over Lago Argentino with a wall about 5 km wide and up to 70 metres high, in shades from pure white to turquoise.\nFrom the Panoramic Point, walk down the walkways facing the glacier and listen to the ice constantly cracking and falling. Then the Safari Náutico, a navigation of about one hour on Brazo Rico, brings you close to the ice wall, where the boat stops for a few minutes to contemplate its immensity. Return to the hotel.",
